## Data quality rules

Contract rules come from `config/contracts.yaml`; business rules are plain SQL in `sql/checks/`. **No row is ever deleted.** Each failing row goes to `dq_exceptions` with the table, row id, key, check, reason and severity. Rows with a high or medium exception are *quarantined* (kept, but left out of the `clean_*` views).

| Check | What it catches | Severity | Rows flagged |
|---|---|---|---:|
| `duplicate_key` | same primary key twice (every copy after the first) | high (medium for review ids) | {{ exceptions.by_check_name.duplicate_key? | int }} |
| `required_null` | a required column is empty | high | {{ exceptions.by_check_name.required_null? | int }} |
| `type_mismatch` | value cannot be cast to the contract type (e.g. `abc` as a price) | high | {{ exceptions.by_check_name.type_mismatch? | int }} |
