## Reconciliation logic

For every `order_id` seen in **any** of orders, order items or payments:

- **Sold (system A)** = sum of `price + freight_value` over the order's items
- **Paid (system B)** = sum of `payment_value` over the order's payments
- **Gap** = paid - sold, **absolute gap** = |gap|, **gap %** = gap / sold
- **Matched** if |gap| <= R$ {{ match_tolerance_brl | num2 }}

Amounts are cast to `DECIMAL(12,2)`, not float, so cents add up exactly.

**Mismatches were investigated before any bucket was defined.** The buckets below each rest on a pattern found in the data, saved as a CSV in `reports/evidence/`. Rules run top to bottom and the first match wins, so every order lands in exactly one bucket.

| Bucket | Rule | Evidence | Orders | Absolute gap |
|---|---|---|---:|---:|
| rounding | 2+ items and \|gap\| <= 1 cent x item count | every gap between 2 and 10 cents is on a multi-item order (`rounding_by_item_count.csv`) | {{ reconciliation.by_category.rounding.orders? | int }} | {{ reconciliation.by_category.rounding.abs_gap_brl? | brl }} |
| voucher_related | a voucher is one of the payments | all are card + voucher splits that overshoot the total (`voucher_orders.csv`) | {{ reconciliation.by_category.voucher_related.orders? | int }} | {{ reconciliation.by_category.voucher_related.abs_gap_brl? | brl }} |
| installment_interest | paid > sold, credit card only, 2+ installments | median overpayment climbs from {{ reconciliation.interest.median_gap_pct_2x | pct }} at 2 installments to {{ reconciliation.interest.median_gap_pct_12x | pct }} at 12; {{ reconciliation.interest.on_shared_ratio_pct | pct }} of these orders share one of {{ reconciliation.interest.shared_ratios | int }} exact paid/sold ratios: a rate table (`interest_rate_card.csv`) | {{ reconciliation.by_category.installment_interest.orders? | int }} | {{ reconciliation.by_category.installment_interest.abs_gap_brl? | brl }} |
| untracked_discount | paid < sold by exactly 5% or 10% of product price | shortfalls land on 5.00% or 10.00% of price; debit card mostly 5%, credit card 10% (`discount_share_of_price.csv`) | {{ reconciliation.by_category.untracked_discount.orders? | int }} | {{ reconciliation.by_category.untracked_discount.abs_gap_brl? | brl }} |
| missing_items | payment exists, no items | {{ reconciliation.missing_items.canceled_or_unavailable_pct | pct }} are canceled or unavailable orders (`missing_items_by_status.csv`) | {{ reconciliation.by_category.missing_items.orders? | int }} | {{ reconciliation.by_category.missing_items.abs_gap_brl? | brl }} |
| missing_payment | items exist, no payment | direct | {{ reconciliation.by_category.missing_payment.orders? | int }} | {{ reconciliation.by_category.missing_payment.abs_gap_brl? | brl }} |
| orphan_no_order | items/payments for an order_id not in orders | direct | {{ reconciliation.by_category.orphan_no_order.orders? | int }} | {{ reconciliation.by_category.orphan_no_order.abs_gap_brl? | brl }} |
| unexplained | none of the above | these need a person | {{ reconciliation.by_category.unexplained.orders? | int }} | {{ reconciliation.by_category.unexplained.abs_gap_brl? | brl }} |

Also checked and ruled out: {{ reconciliation.sequence_gaps.orders_with_sequence_gap | int }} orders have holes in `payment_sequential`, which looked like missing payment rows, but {{ reconciliation.sequence_gaps.still_matched | int }} of them still reconcile to the cent. So a sequence gap is logged as low severity, not treated as missing money.

Window functions (`sql/reconciliation/03_gap_rankings.sql`): `DENSE_RANK()` ranks the biggest gap per purchase month and per state, a running `SUM() OVER` gives each order's cumulative share of all unmatched money, and `LAG()` gives the month-over-month change in unmatched orders. Result: **{{ reconciliation.pareto.orders_for_80pct_of_gap | int }} orders ({{ reconciliation.pareto.pct_of_unmatched_orders | pct1 }} of unmatched) hold 80% of the unmatched money.**

